# W-value Analysis (Hexagonal, Amorphous, Water)

This note explains how to run the Geant4 W-value scan with `wvalue_ice.in` for:
- hexagonal ice
- amorphous ice
- liquid water (Geant4-DNA baseline)

## 1) Prerequisites

- Build `dnaphysics` in:
  - `geant4_projects/dnaphysics-ice/build`
- Ensure Geant4 low-energy data are available (example path in this repo):
  - `G4LEDATA=/Users/yoffegid/Weizmann Institute Dropbox/Gidi Yoffe/Eureka Science/Code/geant4_projects/g4_custom_ice/install/share/Geant4/data/G4EMLOW8.6.1`
- Macro used here:
  - `geant4_projects/dnaphysics-ice/wvalue_ice.in`

## 2) Run Commands

From repository root:

### Hexagonal ice
```bash
cd geant4_projects/dnaphysics-ice/build && \
DNA_PHYSICS=ice_hex DNA_WVALUE_FILE=wvalue_hex_10MeV.txt \
./dnaphysics ../wvalue_ice.in 12
```

### Amorphous ice
```bash
cd geant4_projects/dnaphysics-ice/build && \
DNA_PHYSICS=ice_am DNA_WVALUE_FILE=wvalue_am_10MeV.txt \
./dnaphysics ../wvalue_ice.in 12
```

### Water (same model family as Geant4 wvalue `dna_opt4`)
```bash
cd geant4_projects/dnaphysics-ice/build && \
DNA_PHYSICS=water DNA_WVALUE_FILE=wvalue_water_10MeV.txt \
./dnaphysics ../wvalue_ice.in 12
```

## 2.1) Nominal phase densities (ice physics)

When `DNA_PHYSICS` is set to an ice phase (`ice_hex` or `ice_am`) and material is set to `G4_WATER`, the simulation now
applies phase-dependent nominal density automatically:

- `DNA_PHYSICS=ice_hex` -> `0.917 g/cm3`
- `DNA_PHYSICS=ice_am` -> `0.94 g/cm3`

You can still override manually via `/dna/test/setMatDens ...` if needed.

## 3) Output Files

- W-value text output (append mode):
  - `wvalue_hex_10MeV.txt`
  - `wvalue_am_10MeV.txt`
  - `wvalue_water_10MeV.txt`
- Row format:
  - `E0[eV]  <Nion>  rms(Nion)  w[eV]  w_err[eV]`

If you rerun, rows are appended. To start clean:
```bash
rm -f geant4_projects/dnaphysics-ice/build/wvalue_*_10MeV.txt
```

## 4) Logging Mode

`wvalue_ice.in` currently sets:
- `/dna/test/setLogMode minimal`

So ROOT output stays compact (minimal analysis columns only) while W-value text output is still produced.

## 5) Important Water Caveat

For `DNA_PHYSICS=water` with `dna_opt4`, the current ionisation counting logic is reliable only up to about `1 MeV`.
Above that, standard `eIoni` dominates and the discrete DNA-ionisation counter undercounts, causing unphysical W at high energy.

Recommended for water:
- use `wvalue` points up to `1e6 eV` for physically meaningful W.
